# Formats staged files, then lints them report-only.
#
# oxlint is NOT run with --deny-warnings: every rule in .oxlintrc.json is configured
# as "warn", so treating warnings as fatal contradicts the project's own lint policy
# and blocks commits on a large pre-existing upstream backlog. `pnpm check:lint`
# enforces the per-package --max-warnings budgets; that is the real gate.
#
# --fix is deliberately not used here either: oxlint's react-hooks/exhaustive-deps
# autofix strips `ref.current` from dependency arrays, which silently breaks effects
# that early-return on a null ref. Run `pnpm fix:lint` deliberately instead.
#
# Errors (parse failures and any rule raised to "error") still block the commit.
pnpm lint-staged
